---
/**
 * hubStudio for manufacturers  ·  /solutions/manufacturers
 *
 * From CAD file to finished content. The studio takes CAD files, prototype
 * photos or product data and delivers images, film and launch material
 * (Studio only, the highlighted way); marketing can use the app for its own
 * product pictures and posts; Studio + app keeps engineering sign-off on
 * record in Validation. The retired "We Build It For You" offer is gone;
 * the FAQ now explains the three ways to work.
 * Copy from the content-quality-us deck (cq/sol-manufacturers).
 *
 * Per repo standards: no em dash character, no decorative numerals inside
 * cards or repeated blocks, body copy at var(--type-body), hubStudio keeps
 * its canonical lowercase-h casing.
 */
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Button from '../../components/Button.astro';
import WaysToWork from '../../components/WaysToWork.astro';
import DualCta from '../../components/DualCta.astro';
import AppShot from '../../components/AppShot.astro';
import { appShots } from '../../data/app-shots';
import { APP_SIGNUP, BRIEF_URL } from '../../lib/links';

const SITE = 'https://www.hubstudio.ai';

const colourBar = [
  '#e94e1b', '#c73e10', '#1e3a8a', '#0e1f4e', '#0e1633',
  '#6b6b73', '#a8a299', '#d8d3cb', '#e5e1db', '#ffffff',
];

/* The bottleneck, as three plain sentences. No labels, no ordinals. */
const reasons = [
  {
    title: 'Engineers end up at the wrong desk.',
    body: 'The people who designed the product end up making renders and screenshots for marketing, instead of the next product.',
  },
  {
    title: 'The versions drift apart.',
    body: 'Marketing, sales, and dealers each hold a different picture of the product. Nobody is sure which one is current.',
  },
  {
    title: 'The launch waits.',
    body: 'Content arrives after the product. Dealers sell from last year’s catalog, and sales starts late.',
  },
];

/* What the studio makes from your files. Images kept from the previous page. */
const lanes = [
  {
    label: 'Product visuals from CAD',
    heading: 'Photoreal product images, made from your CAD files.',
    image: '/Images/pmd-inspect.jpg',
    alt: 'A documentary frame of a manufacturing engineer reviewing CAD-derived assembly guides on a calibrated monitor, warm window light from camera left, lifted black point.',
    body: 'Often before the first unit comes off the line. Materials and finishes follow your references.',
    tags: ['CAD-based imagery', 'Exploded views', '360-degree views', 'Finish and color variants'],
  },
  {
    label: 'Launch material',
    heading: 'Ready while the product is still in production.',
    image: '/Images/pmd-factory.jpg',
    alt: 'A wide shop-floor frame of a partially assembled product on a rig with calibrated daylight from a tall window, prime-lens depth of field, warm shadow grade.',
    body: 'Dealer catalogs, training visuals, and a launch film. We can localize each piece for the markets you sell in.',
    tags: ['Dealer catalogs', 'Training visuals', 'Launch films', 'Localized versions'],
  },
  {
    label: 'Products in context',
    heading: 'The machine where your customers use it.',
    image: '/Images/md-launch.jpg',
    alt: 'A wide industrial environment with a piece of equipment in context, single low-angle directional light, calibrated negative space for headline copy, real-photography grade.',
    body: 'A machine shown in the kind of plant where your customers work, without moving it anywhere.',
    tags: ['Application scenes', 'Trade-show visuals', 'Sales presentations', 'Vertical-market versions'],
  },
  {
    label: 'Documentation visuals',
    heading: 'Assembly, maintenance, and safety visuals.',
    image: '/Images/md-fmcg.jpg',
    alt: 'A precise close-up of a compliance label and a printed safety instruction sheet on a workshop bench, hard side light, real-photography grade.',
    body: 'Drawn from your approved source files. Your engineers and your compliance team sign them off. The certification itself stays with your team.',
    tags: ['Assembly visuals', 'Maintenance guides', 'Safety sheet visuals', 'Revision updates'],
  },
];

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'Can you make product visuals from CAD before production?',
    a: 'Yes. We work from CAD exports, prototype photos, and spec sheets to make product images, launch material, and film while the product is still in production. Tell us the file formats you have and we’ll say what we need.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Do you replace our content team?',
    a: 'No. The studio takes the volume and the craft work so your engineers can stay engineers. Your marketing team keeps the brand, the calendar, and the final say.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Which way should we work with you?',
    a: 'There are three. With Studio only, you send a brief and get finished files back, with no account needed. With Studio + app, we make the work inside hubStudio and your people approve it there. With Use the app, your own team makes and publishes the work. Most manufacturers start with Studio only and add the app when marketing wants to make its own posts.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How do you keep technical details right?',
    a: 'We work from your engineering files and references, and your engineers approve every asset before it’s used. If they spot an error, they send the piece back with a comment and the fix arrives as a new version. With Studio + app, all of that stays on record in Validation.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can you localize for other markets?',
    a: 'Yes. We adapt settings, signage, and on-screen text for each market you sell in, and with Studio + app your local teams can review in the same thread.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What can you make for us?',
    a: 'Product images and 360-degree views, exploded and assembly visuals, maintenance and safety visuals, dealer catalogs, trade-show material, training visuals, launch films, and short product videos.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Does it connect to our DAM, PIM, or ERP?',
    a: 'The app has no connectors. For studio work, we work from your exports and deliver finished files in the formats and sizes your systems need.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How is it priced?',
    a: 'The studio is priced per asset, per project, or on retainer, and quoted after a brief. The app runs on a prepaid balance with no subscription and no seat fees; you see the price before every run.',
  },
];

const faqSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faqs.map((f) => ({
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: f.q,
    acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: f.a },
  })),
};

const breadcrumbSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
  itemListElement: [
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: SITE },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Solutions', item: `${SITE}/solutions` },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: 'Manufacturers', item: `${SITE}/solutions/manufacturers` },
  ],
};

const arrow = 'M4 10h12M11 5l5 5-5 5';
---

<Layout
  title="hubStudio for manufacturers: from CAD file to content"
  description="Manufacturers send CAD files or product data to our studio and get finished images and film back. Marketing can use the app for its own posts."
>
  <script is:inline type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(breadcrumbSchema)} />
  <script is:inline type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema)} />

  <div class="prog" aria-hidden="true"><span class="prog__bar"></span></div>

  <div class="page">
    <!-- ============ HERO ============ -->
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="hero__panel">
        <svg class="hero__reg" viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true">
          <circle cx="50" cy="50" r="34" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" />
          <path d="M50 4v92M4 50h92" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" />
        </svg>
        <div class="hero__panel-in">
          <p class="kicker kicker--light r">
            <span class="kicker__tick"></span>Solutions
            <span class="kicker__sep">/</span> Manufacturers
          </p>
          <h1 class="hero__title">
            <span class="line"><span class="line__i">From CAD file</span></span>
            <span class="line"><span class="line__i">to finished</span></span>
            <span class="line"><span class="line__i serif">content.</span></span>
          </h1>
          <p class="hero__tag r" style="--d:.45s">
            Your engineers get back to <em>engineering</em>.
          </p>
          <div class="hero__lead r" style="--d:.55s">
            <p>
              A new product is signed off. Then marketing wants pictures and
              sales wants a sheet. Every dealer wants the lot in its own
              language. Before long, a design engineer is exporting renders at
              9 p.m.
            </p>
            <p>
              Our studio takes CAD files, prototype photos, or product data
              and makes finished images, film, and launch material. You don’t
              need an account for that. Your marketing team can use the
              hubStudio app for its own product pictures and posts.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="hero__cta r" style="--d:.65s">
            <Button variant="primary" href={`${BRIEF_URL}?way=studio`}>Send a brief</Button>
            <a class="ghost-link ghost-link--light" href={APP_SIGNUP} rel="noopener">
              Create your account
              <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d={arrow} fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" />
              </svg>
            </a>
          </div>
          <p class="hero__meta r" style="--d:.72s">
            CAD <span>/</span> Product data <span>/</span> Launch material
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero__visual">
        <img
          src="/Images/manufacturers-hero.jpg"
          alt="A wide shop-floor frame of a partially assembled industrial product under tall window light, prime-lens depth of field, warm shadow grade, calibrated stations and engineering reference sheets pinned along the back wall."
          width="1024"
          height="1024"
          loading="eager"
          fetchpriority="high"
        />
        <span class="hero__chip">Manufacturing <span>/</span> Launch prep</span>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="cbar" aria-hidden="true">
      {colourBar.map((c) => <span style={`background:${c}`}></span>)}
    </div>

    <!-- ============ WHY ============ -->
    <section class="why">
      <div class="shell">
        <header class="band band--split">
          <div>
            <p class="kicker kicker--light r"><span class="kicker__tick"></span>The bottleneck</p>
            <h2 class="dh r" style="--d:.05s">
              The content cost<br />nobody <span class="serif">measures</span>.
            </h2>
          </div>
          <p class="band__note band__note--light r" style="--d:.1s">
            You won’t find it on a budget line. You find it when a launch sits
            waiting for its pictures.
          </p>
        </header>

        <div class="reasons">
          {
            reasons.map((r, i) => (
              <article class="reason r" style={`--d:${i * 0.08}s`}>
                <span class="reason__tick" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                <h3 class="reason__title">{r.title}</h3>
                <p class="reason__body">{r.body}</p>
              </article>
            ))
          }
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ STUDIO: FROM YOUR FILES ============ -->
    <section class="cover" id="studio">
      <div class="shell">
        <header class="band">
          <p class="kicker r"><span class="kicker__tick"></span>Studio only</p>
          <h2 class="dh r" style="--d:.05s">
            From your files to<br />finished <span class="serif">work</span>.
          </h2>
          <p class="band__note r" style="--d:.1s">
            This is the usual first step. Send what you have: CAD exports,
            material and color references, prototype photos, spec sheets. A
            producer reads it within one business day and tells you what else
            we’d need.
          </p>
        </header>

        {
          lanes.map((c, i) => (
            <article class={`feature ${i % 2 === 1 ? 'feature--rev' : ''}`}>
              <figure class="feature__media crop r-clip">
                <div class="crop__inner">
                  <img src={c.image} alt={c.alt} width="1024" height="1024" loading="lazy" />
                </div>
                <figcaption class="fig">{c.label}</figcaption>
              </figure>
              <div class="feature__body">
                <p class="feature__idx r">
                  <span class="feature__tick"></span>
                  {c.label}
                </p>
                <h3 class="dh dh--sm r" style="--d:.05s">{c.heading}</h3>
                <p class="feature__p r" style="--d:.1s">{c.body}</p>
                <p class="feature__scope r" style="--d:.16s">In scope</p>
                <ul class="chips r" style="--d:.2s">
                  {c.tags.map((t) => (
                    <li class="chip">{t}</li>
                  ))}
                </ul>
              </div>
            </article>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ THE APP ============ -->
    <section class="appsec" id="app">
      <div class="shell appsec__grid">
        <div class="appsec__body">
          <p class="kicker r"><span class="kicker__tick"></span>Use the app</p>
          <h2 class="dh r" style="--d:.05s">
            Your team’s own<br />pictures and <span class="serif">posts</span>.
          </h2>
          <p class="appsec__p r" style="--d:.1s">
            Not everything needs a brief. Your marketing team can make a
            product picture for a trade-show post, crop a studio image to a
            LinkedIn format, or draft the post with “Draft with AI”. Then it
            goes straight to the company page.
          </p>
          <p class="appsec__p r" style="--d:.14s">
            Files live in the Assets Library, in folders, with tags, and with
            versions, so the approved picture is the one everyone finds. You
            pay only for what you run, and the Image editor costs nothing to
            use. Engineers who only need to look can join as Viewers, who see
            the team’s work and spend nothing.
          </p>
          <p class="r" style="--d:.18s">
            <a class="ghost-link" href="/app">
              See what the app does
              <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d={arrow} fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" />
              </svg>
            </a>
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="appsec__shots">
          <div class="r" style="--d:.08s">
            <AppShot shot={appShots.linkedin} path="/social/linkedin/posts" caption />
          </div>
          <div class="r" style="--d:.14s">
            <AppShot shot={appShots.libraryActions} path="/files" caption />
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ THREE WAYS TO WORK ============ -->
    <WaysToWork
      tone="white"
      highlight="studio"
      pre="Three ways to work with "
      accent="us"
      post="."
      lead="The studio comes first for many of the manufacturers we work with. Some add the app for the marketing team, and some have the studio work inside the app so engineers can sign off there."
    />

    <!-- ============ STUDIO + APP: SIGN-OFF ON RECORD ============ -->
    <section class="record" id="approvals">
      <div class="shell record__grid">
        <div class="record__body">
          <p class="kicker kicker--light r"><span class="kicker__tick"></span>Studio + app</p>
          <h2 class="dh r" style="--d:.05s">
            A sign-off your<br />engineers can <span class="serif">trace</span>.
          </h2>
          <p class="record__lead r" style="--d:.08s">
            If your engineers want a say before anything ships, this part is
            for them.
          </p>
          <p class="record__p r" style="--d:.12s">
            With Studio + app, our creatives make the work inside hubStudio.
            Your engineers and marketers approve it in Validation, or send it
            back with a comment.
          </p>
          <p class="record__p r" style="--d:.16s">
            Each version sits on one thread, and nothing on that thread can be
            deleted. When a dealer asks whether the exploded view matches
            revision C, you can show who approved it and when.
          </p>
          <p class="record__p r" style="--d:.2s">
            For a manufacturer, working in your own workspace usually makes
            sense: you add our creatives as members, and every file stays in
            your History and Assets Library when the project ends.
          </p>
          <p class="record__more r" style="--d:.24s">
            <a class="ghost-link ghost-link--light" href="/studio/with-the-app">
              How Studio + app works
              <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d={arrow} fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" />
              </svg>
            </a>
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="record__media r" style="--d:.1s">
          <AppShot shot={appShots.validationSend} path="/validation" caption dark />
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ WHY HUBSTUDIO ============ -->
    <section class="source">
      <div class="shell source__grid">
        <div class="source__visual">
          <figure class="source__main crop">
            <div class="crop__inner">
              <img
                src="/Images/who-we-are-studio.jpg"
                alt="A documentary frame of the hubStudio floor with calibrated stations, engineering proofs along the back wall and a quiet review session at one of the central monitors."
                width="1360"
                height="768"
                loading="lazy"
              />
            </div>
          </figure>
          <div class="source__stat">
            <span class="source__stat-num">48 hours</span>
            <span class="source__stat-cap">A written proposal after your brief</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="source__body">
          <p class="kicker kicker--light r"><span class="kicker__tick"></span>Why hubStudio</p>
          <h2 class="dh r" style="--d:.05s">
            A production team that<br />can read a CAD <span class="serif">file</span>.
          </h2>
          <p class="source__lead r" style="--d:.1s">
            Senior art directors lead every brief, with AI production
            underneath. Some assets are rendered or shot, others generated.
          </p>
          <p class="source__p r" style="--d:.16s">
            Two jobs show how this works. For a premium SUV, we built <a class="source__a" href="/work/premium-suv">the launch imagery for each market</a> without shipping the car anywhere. For iFlytek’s AI wearable, <a class="source__a" href="/work/iflytek-anypin">one launch film</a> mixed live shooting, CGI, and AIGC, then was cut for every channel.
          </p>
          <p class="source__p r" style="--d:.22s">
            We record the provenance of every asset, so you can tell how each
            one was made. The studio was founded by Cyril Drouin, former CEO
            at Publicis.
          </p>
          <ul class="creds r" style="--d:.28s">
            {
              ['CAD to content', 'Senior art directors', 'Provenance per asset', 'Approvals on record'].map((c) => (
                <li class="cred">
                  <svg viewBox="0 0 14 14" aria-hidden="true">
                    <path d="M2 7.5 5.5 11 12 3.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" />
                  </svg>
                  {c}
                </li>
              ))
            }
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ FAQ ============ -->
    <section class="faq" id="faq">
      <div class="shell faq__grid">
        <aside class="faq__intro">
          <p class="kicker r"><span class="kicker__tick"></span>Questions</p>
          <h2 class="dh r" style="--d:.05s">
            Before the<br />first <span class="serif">unit</span>.
          </h2>
          <p class="faq__sub r" style="--d:.1s">
            What engineering and marketing leads ask us first.
          </p>
          <p class="faq__updated r" style="--d:.12s">Updated September 2026</p>
          <div class="r" style="--d:.16s">
            <Button variant="primary" href={`${BRIEF_URL}?way=studio`}>Send a brief</Button>
          </div>
        </aside>

        <div class="acc">
          {
            faqs.map((faq) => (
              <div class="acc__row r">
                <button class="acc__q" type="button" aria-expanded="false">
                  <span class="acc__qmark">Q</span>
                  <span class="acc__qtext">{faq.q}</span>
                  <span class="acc__icon" aria-hidden="true">
                    <span></span><span></span>
                  </span>
                </button>
                <div class="acc__a">
                  <div class="acc__a-inner">
                    <p>{faq.a}</p>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            ))
          }
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ CLOSING ============ -->
    <DualCta
      lead="studio"
      briefQuery="way=studio"
      pre="Send us the "
      accent="files"
      post="."
      text="A CAD set, a launch date, or just the product line you want to move next. A producer reads your brief within one business day. Or open the app for your marketing team, at no cost."
    />
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .page { --ink: #0e1633; --navy: #0e1f4e; --paper: #f0ede9; --paper-2: #e7e3dd; overflow: clip; }
  .shell { width: 100%; max-width: 1280px; margin-inline: auto; padding-inline: clamp(22px, 5vw, 60px); }
  .prog { position: fixed; inset: 0 0 auto 0; height: 3px; z-index: 200; pointer-events: none; }
  .prog__bar { display: block; height: 100%; width: 100%; transform: scaleX(0); transform-origin: 0 50%; background: var(--brand-orange); }
  .r, .r-clip { --d: 0s; }
  .r { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(26px); transition: opacity 0.7s ease, transform 0.8s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1); transition-delay: var(--d); }
  .r.in { opacity: 1; transform: none; }
  .r-clip .crop__inner { clip-path: inset(0 0 101% 0); transition: clip-path 1.05s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1); transition-delay: var(--d, 0s); }
  .r-clip .crop__inner img { transform: scale(1.12); transition: transform 1.3s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1); transition-delay: var(--d, 0s); }
  .r-clip.in .crop__inner { clip-path: inset(0 0 0 0); }
  .r-clip.in .crop__inner img { transform: scale(1); }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .r, .r.in { opacity: 1; transform: none; transition: none; }
    .r-clip .crop__inner, .r-clip .crop__inner img { clip-path: none; transform: none; transition: none; }
  }
  .kicker { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 9px; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: 0.16em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--text-mute); }
  .kicker--light { color: rgba(240, 237, 233, 0.66); }
  .kicker__tick { width: 22px; height: 0; border-top: 1.5px solid var(--brand-orange); }
  .kicker__sep { color: var(--brand-orange); }
  .dh { font-family: var(--font-sans); font-weight: 600; font-size: clamp(34px, 4.4vw, 62px); line-height: 1.02; letter-spacing: -0.03em; }
  .dh--sm { font-size: clamp(26px, 2.6vw, 38px); }
  .serif { font-family: var(--font-serif); font-style: italic; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: -0.01em; color: var(--brand-orange); }
  .crop { position: relative; margin: 0; }
  .crop::before, .crop::after { content: ''; position: absolute; width: 16px; height: 16px; z-index: 2; }
  .crop::before { top: -9px; left: -9px; border-top: 1.5px solid var(--brand-orange); border-left: 1.5px solid var(--brand-orange); }
  .crop::after { right: -9px; bottom: 28px; border-right: 1.5px solid var(--brand-orange); border-bottom: 1.5px solid var(--brand-orange); }
  .crop__inner { overflow: hidden; border-radius: 4px; }
  .crop__inner img { display: block; width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; }
  .fig { margin-top: 14px; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--text-mute); }
  .ghost-link { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 9px; font-size: var(--type-small); font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-ink); }
  .ghost-link svg { flex: none; width: 19px; height: 19px; transition: transform 0.24s ease-out; }
  .ghost-link:hover svg { transform: translateX(5px); }
  .ghost-link--light { color: var(--text-on-dark); }
  .band { max-width: 720px; margin-bottom: clamp(40px, 5vw, 70px); display: grid; gap: 18px; }
  .band--split { max-width: none; grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  @media (min-width: 880px) {
    .band--split { grid-template-columns: 1fr 0.82fr; align-items: end; gap: 18px 60px; }
    .band--split > div { display: grid; gap: 18px; }
  }
  .band__note { font-size: var(--type-lead); line-height: 1.5; color: var(--text-mute); }
  .band__note--light { color: rgba(240, 237, 233, 0.76); }
  .cbar { display: flex; height: 12px; }
  .cbar span { flex: 1; }
  .hero { display: grid; background: var(--ink); color: var(--text-on-dark); }
